-- title:
--   Pinned α bounded by trivial steps of an admissible chain
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes with $q \neq 2$ and $q$ dividing the Eisenstein numerator $(p-1)/\gcd(p-1,12)$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, and let $S$ be a primary Néron torsion-sheaf datum `JZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionSheaf p q A hA`, consisting of a core, a family of finite flat models and a family of pinned invariants. Write $J_0(p)$ for `JZero p`, the group of degree-zero divisor classes of the base-changed modular function field of level $p$, equipped with the `HeckeAlg`-module structure `heckeModuleBar p`, and for each $m$ let $E_m$ be `eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar p q m`, the intersection of the kernel of multiplication by $q^m$ on $J_0(p)$ with the union over $k$ of the subgroups killed by the $k$-th power of the Eisenstein maximal ideal `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q` (the contraction along `eisensteinEval p` of the ideal generated by $q$). Assume given, for each $m$, an `OpenAction` $\Phi_m$ on $E_m$, that is, a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to the additive automorphisms of $E_m$ with open kernel, such that $\Phi_m(\sigma)x$ coincides in $J_0(p)$ with $\sigma \cdot x$ for all $\sigma$ and all $x \in E_m$; and an admissible chain $c_m$ of length $n$ for $\Phi_m$ at $q$: an increasing chain of additive subgroups of $E_m$ from $\bot$ to $\top$, each successive quotient of cardinality $q$, with each step tagged by a Boolean, a step tagged `true` satisfying $\Phi_m(\sigma)x - x$ lies in the preceding subgroup for all $\sigma$ and all $x$ in the larger subgroup, and a step tagged `false` satisfying $\Phi_m(\sigma)x - a\,x$ lies in the preceding subgroup whenever $\sigma\zeta = \zeta^{a}$ for a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$. Then for every $m$ the invariant $\alpha$ attached to level $m$ by the pinned-invariant component of $S$ is at most `filtAlpha (c m)`, the number of indices whose tag is `true`.
--
--   This is Mazur's comparison between the $\alpha$-invariant read off from the finite flat model at $q$ of the Eisenstein-primary $q^m$-torsion of $J_0(p)$ and the number of constituents of multiplicative (trivially acted upon) type in any admissible filtration of that torsion group; the bound is one half of the equality used to control the growth of $\alpha$ with $m$. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.jZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_growth_v5`](thm.html#ModularCurve.jZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_growth_v5).
